  <div class="main-content-container" style="z-index:5;position:relative;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;line-height:1.38;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:right;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Exhibit 99.1</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;line-height:1.38;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:center;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;line-height:1.38;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><img src="img212243993_0.jpg" alt="img212243993_0.jpg" style="vertical-align:bottom;width:132px;height:29px;"></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:12pt;margin-top:10pt;line-height:1.38;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:right;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:12pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">News Release</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:13.5pt;margin-top:10pt;line-height:1.38;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:center;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:13.5pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">     RAMBUS REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2026 FINANCIAL RESULTS</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;line-height:1.15;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;line-height:1.38;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Times New Roman;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.333%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#x2022;</font><div style="display:inline;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Record quarterly revenue of $218.3 million, up 22% year over year, exceeding guidance range</font></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;line-height:1.38;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Times New Roman;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.333%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#x2022;</font><div style="display:inline;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">GAAP diluted earnings per share of $0.69 and non-GAAP diluted earnings per share of $0.84, exceeding guidance range</font></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;line-height:1.38;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Times New Roman;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.333%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#x2022;</font><div style="display:inline;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Record product revenue of $114.3 million, up 15% quarter over quarter and 22% year over year</font></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="tab-size:32px;display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;line-height:1.38;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Times New Roman;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:3.333%;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:3.333%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#x2022;</font><div style="display:inline;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Expanded product and IP offerings for next-generation AI systems, including industry-leading PMIC for LPDDR6 SOCAMM2 and data center-class Root of Trust security IP</font></div></div><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:10pt;line-height:1.38;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">SAN JOSE, Calif. </font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#x2013;</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> October 26, 2026 </font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#x2013; Rambus Inc. (NASDAQ:RMBS), a provider of industry-leading chips and IP making data faster and safer, today reported financial results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026. Total revenue for the third quarter was $218.3 million, product revenue was $114.3 million, royalties revenue was $77.0 million and contract and other revenue was $27.0 million. GAAP diluted earnings per share was $0.69 and non-GAAP diluted earnings per share was $0.84. The Company also generated a record $102.5 million of cash from operating activities in the third quarter.</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:10pt;line-height:1.38;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Management Commentary</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:10pt;line-height:1.38;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#x201c;Rambus delivered record quarterly revenue and earnings that exceeded our guidance, with strong customer demand driving record product revenue and record cash from operations,&#x201d; said Luc Seraphin, president and chief executive officer of Rambus. &#x201c;We continue to expand our product and IP offerings to address the growing performance requirements of next-generation AI and data center infrastructure. Through ongoing execution on our roadmap and accelerating demand for our differentiated solutions, we expect an even stronger performance in Q4 and are well positioned to deliver long-term profitable growth and value for our stockholders.&#x201d;</font></p>
